Presentation of variables: * -- Mean (SD) (optional), Median [Q1, Q3] and Min - Max; † -- absolute frequency (percent).

\
Most studies (88%) were published after 2009 and had a retrospective design (85%). Ileostomies were used in almost 60% of studies, ileostomy or colostomy in 40%, and colostomy alone in only 2.7%. Fifty percent of studies had a sample size within the interquartile range of 100 to 539, with a maximum of 17,867. Estimated pooled values were: mean male proportion 61%, mean age 62 years, mean BMI 24.7 kg/m², and mean LOS 10.9 days; median relative rates were NACh(R)Th 50%, overall complications 30%, severe complications 9.4%, anastomotic leak 5.6%, infection 10.1%, and mortality 0.7%. However, much of the data were unavailable across studies (cumulative absolute counts were not reported, not assessed, or only relative results were presented).


