Figure 1. Forest plot for pooled incidence of anastomotic leak. 
```{r}
#| label: 3-forest-al-overall
#| fig-width: 9
#| fig-height: 16

m.prop <- df |> 
 filter_out(is.na(`Anastomotic leak`)) |> 
 mutate(`Publication Year` = factor(ifelse(`Publication Year` < 2010, "<2010",
                                    ifelse(`Publication Year` >= 2020, "≥2020", "2010-2019")),
                                    levels = c("<2010", "2010-2019", "≥2020"))) |> 
 metaprop(event = `Anastomotic leak`,
          n = N,
          studlab = Author_year,
          data = _,
          method = "GLMM",
          sm = "PLOGIT",
          common = F,
          random = T,
          prediction = T,
          method.random.ci = "HK",
          method.predict = "HTS")

forest(m.prop, 
       common = F, 
       random = T, 
       overall = T, 
       prediction = T,
       pooled.totals = T, 
       pooled.events = T, 
       backtransf = T,
       print.I2.ci = T, 
       print.tau2.ci = F,
       pscale = 100,
       xlim = c(0, 30),
       at = seq(0, 30, 5),
       smlab = "",
       xlab = "Anastomotic leak, %",
       leftcols = c("studlab", "n", "event"),
       leftlabs = c("Author, Year (subset)", "N sample", "Events"),
       rightcols = c("effect", "ci"),
       rightlabs = c("Proportion, %", "95% CI"),
       digits = 2,
       fontsize = 10,
       spacing = 1,
       col.square = "grey75",
       col.diamond.random = "blue",
       col.predict = "red"
       )
```
Diamond -- pooled effect, vertical reference line -- pooled estimate.

\
A total of 26534 patients and 2443 events were included. Statistical heterogeneity was high: I² = 87.3% (95% CI 84.6; 89.6), τ² = 0.4086 (p < 0.0001). In the random-effects model, the pooled incidence of anastomotic leak was 7.12% (95% CI 6.03; 8.4), with a prediction interval of 2.07%; 21.78%. On average, the expected rate of anastomotic leak after TME with primary anastomosis and a defunctioning stoma is around 7%, but in a new study the observed rate could reasonably range from 2% to 21%.

